WEBVTT

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:12.369
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning all. You alright? Let's get started, quick stand-up for Monday. Just run round the board and pick up anything live for today.</v>

00:00:13.529 --> 00:00:20.179
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Morning. Bit nippy in here again, by the way, the heating in the portakabin is still doing basically nothing.</v>

00:00:21.399 --> 00:00:26.300
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, I was gonna say, fingers don't work till about half eight in there.</v>

00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:32.799
<v Tomasz Nowak>Could be worse, there's a birthday cake in the office, so at least morale's covered.</v>

00:00:34.049 --> 00:00:35.250
<v Fiona Doyle>Whose is it?</v>

00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:40.799
<v Tomasz Nowak>No idea, I just saw it and thought, right, that's my breakfast sorted.</v>

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:45.929
<v Sarah Okafor>Excellent, very professional. Right, actual work. Callum, production first?</v>

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:58.850
<v Callum Reid>Yeah so line 1's fine. Line 2 had that stop again on the robot cell overnight, bit of a jam by the pick head. It's not running clean at the minute.</v>

00:01:00.409 --> 00:01:05.659
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay. We need the jam clearing and the sensors checked on the line 2 robot.</v>

00:01:06.849 --> 00:01:13.849
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, I'll clear the jam and check the sensors on the line 2 robot, should have that done by 11am.</v>

00:01:16.269 --> 00:01:17.469
<v Callum Reid>Nice one.</v>

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:22.189
<v Sarah Okafor>Good, thanks Olumide. Anything else on line 2 while we're there?</v>

00:01:22.819 --> 00:01:30.519
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Just as an aside, I finished the repair on the GT1 compressor last night, so that's done, nothing for today on that.</v>

00:01:32.299 --> 00:01:40.349
<v Marcus Hale>And from my side, I already swapped the filter on the turbine one gas valve yesterday, so that's off the list as well.</v>

00:01:41.230 --> 00:01:43.329
<v Sarah Okafor>Good. Closed jobs, lovely. Hannah, quality?</v>

00:01:45.469 --> 00:01:58.769
<v Hannah Price>Yeah. No fresh NCRs from nights. I did see the pressure on the HV board dip for a few minutes, it came back on its own, so just an observation really, not asking for anything off this call.</v>

00:02:00.069 --> 00:02:11.620
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Funny you say that, I saw the pressure on the number two bearing dip for a few minutes, it came back on its own as well. Same sort of thing, just noting it.</v>

00:02:12.479 --> 00:02:18.080
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, log both, but we're not spinning up new jobs from that now if it's recovered.</v>

00:02:18.860 --> 00:02:26.560
<v Hannah Price>Mm. Also, blocker-wise, the supplier still hasn't confirmed the delivery for the fire panel, so I can't move that one on yet.</v>

00:02:28.969 --> 00:02:31.770
<v Fiona Doyle>I've chased them twice. Still waiting, same position.</v>

00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:38.469
<v Sarah Okafor>Fine, blocked is blocked. Keep chasing, but that's not a task for this morning meeting.</v>

00:02:40.430 --> 00:02:50.229
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Same story on another one, the supplier still hasn't confirmed the delivery for the line two. So I'm a bit stuck there as well till they come back.</v>

00:02:50.819 --> 00:02:52.919
<v Callum Reid>That'll be the replacement bits, yeah?</v>

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:57.530
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, exactly. Can't do much till we've actually got a date.</v>

00:02:58.449 --> 00:02:59.650
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood. Fiona, planning?</v>

00:03:00.590 --> 00:03:08.639
<v Fiona Doyle>Main thing, just so nobody starts stripping anything, we were looking at line 3 work, but I think you've already got that, Sarah.</v>

00:03:10.759 --> 00:03:19.860
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, just to be clear, we were going to replace the belt on the line 3 but that's been pushed to next month so ignore it.</v>

00:03:21.379 --> 00:03:23.479
<v Tomasz Nowak>Happy days, one less filthy job.</v>

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:35.449
<v Sarah Okafor>Don't sound too pleased, Tom. Right, safety side. We still need to update the risk assessment for work on the line 2 interlock, on the 3rd, top priority please.</v>

00:03:37.210 --> 00:03:40.710
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, that's got to be in before the job starts.</v>

00:03:42.159 --> 00:03:47.759
<v Fiona Doyle>I've got the permit pack mostly lined up, but the risk assessment bit needs an owner.</v>

00:03:49.460 --> 00:03:57.159
<v Sarah Okafor>So, update the risk assessment for work on the line 2 interlock, on the 3rd, top priority please. Who can take that?</v>

00:03:59.050 --> 00:04:04.650
<v Tomasz Nowak>I can help with the wording maybe, but I've got my hands full on breakdown follow-ups.</v>

00:04:06.969 --> 00:04:12.569
<v Hannah Price>I'm tied up with audit evidence this morning and supplier chasing. I can't commit to it.</v>

00:04:13.569 --> 00:04:18.819
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Not me, if I'm on the line 2 robot and then the other controls backlog.</v>

00:04:20.490 --> 00:04:25.389
<v Callum Reid>I can give operational input, but I can't sit and own the document today.</v>

00:04:25.899 --> 00:04:36.399
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, okay, noted then: update the risk assessment for work on the line 2 interlock, on the 3rd, top priority please, but nobody's actually picking it up in this meeting.</v>

00:04:38.199 --> 00:04:41.000
<v Fiona Doyle>I'll flag it red on the board then.</v>

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:47.699
<v Sarah Okafor>Do that. Next one, yard and FLT side: I'll do the pre-use checks on the trucks.</v>

00:04:48.110 --> 00:04:51.259
<v Callum Reid>Cheers, that helps, we're a bit thin first thing.</v>

00:04:53.519 --> 00:04:56.670
<v Sarah Okafor>No problem, I'll get those done straight after this.</v>

00:04:58.860 --> 00:05:03.410
<v Sarah Okafor>Tom, while I've got you, toolbox talk for the team still needs sorting.</v>

00:05:05.819 --> 00:05:12.819
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, I'll organise the toolbox talk for the team. Normal priority, I'll just grab them between jobs once everyone's in.</v>

00:05:15.149 --> 00:05:16.350
<v Sarah Okafor>Good man.</v>

00:05:17.810 --> 00:05:23.060
<v Marcus Hale>I've not really got much else from plant. Boilers steady, CHP behaved overnight for once.</v>

00:05:24.439 --> 00:05:29.339
<v Sarah Okafor>Alright. Marcus Hale, can you send the shift handover report round today? No rush.</v>

00:05:31.730 --> 00:05:37.329
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, no problem, I'll send the shift handover report round today. No rush taken literally, yeah?</v>

00:05:38.920 --> 00:05:41.720
<v Sarah Okafor>Ha, within reason. Just before lunch is fine.</v>

00:05:43.290 --> 00:05:44.490
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, fair.</v>

00:05:45.629 --> 00:05:48.779
<v Callum Reid>Anything on staffing? I've got Dan off sick still.</v>

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:56.370
<v Sarah Okafor>I've covered packing with agency for the first half. We'll juggle after ten if needed.</v>

00:05:58.819 --> 00:06:08.620
<v Hannah Price>On line 2, once Olumide's been in, give me a shout if there was product trapped in the cell. I might need to quarantine a couple of trays.</v>

00:06:10.480 --> 00:06:18.879
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, will do. But just to be clear, my bit is the jam and sensor check, not starting a full strip unless it's obvious.</v>

00:06:20.050 --> 00:06:22.149
<v Callum Reid>That's all we need for now.</v>

00:06:23.649 --> 00:06:31.350
<v Fiona Doyle>If line 2 comes back by 11, I can keep the afternoon plan as is. If not, I'll have to reshuffle despatch.</v>

00:06:32.740 --> 00:06:35.889
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, update Fiona once you've had eyes on, Olumide.</v>

00:06:36.329 --> 00:06:37.529
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yep.</v>

00:06:39.699 --> 00:06:44.250
<v Tomasz Nowak>Do you want me to cover anything on permits later, or leave it?</v>

00:06:44.709 --> 00:06:51.709
<v Sarah Okafor>Leave permits for now. Bigger issue is still that risk assessment on the line 2 interlock hasn't got an owner.</v>

00:06:53.329 --> 00:06:58.230
<v Hannah Price>If somebody frees up after lunch we can revisit it, but right now, no.</v>

00:06:59.160 --> 00:07:00.560
<v Callum Reid>Bit tight today, innit.</v>

00:07:02.470 --> 00:07:03.670
<v Marcus Hale>Mondays.</v>

00:07:04.550 --> 00:07:08.750
<v Sarah Okafor>Always. Anything else that's definitely not a task, just so it's heard?</v>

00:07:10.430 --> 00:07:14.629
<v Olumide Adeyemi>No, aside from the supplier thing and that pressure dip, that's me.</v>

00:07:16.899 --> 00:07:20.750
<v Hannah Price>Same here. Fire panel's blocked till the supplier answers, nothing else.</v>

00:07:21.800 --> 00:07:24.600
<v Tomasz Nowak>I've just got routine PMs. And cake management.</v>

00:07:25.139 --> 00:07:26.540
<v Fiona Doyle>Critical support function, that.</v>

00:07:27.670 --> 00:07:35.720
<v Sarah Okafor>Essential service. Right, recap before we drop: Olumide will clear the jam and check the sensors on the line 2 robot by 11am.</v>

00:07:37.189 --> 00:07:38.389
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yep.</v>

00:07:38.910 --> 00:07:41.709
<v Sarah Okafor>I'll do the pre-use checks on the trucks.</v>

00:07:43.879 --> 00:07:47.730
<v Sarah Okafor>Tom will organise the toolbox talk for the team, normal priority.</v>

00:07:49.410 --> 00:07:50.610
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yep, got it.</v>

00:07:52.540 --> 00:07:56.740
<v Sarah Okafor>Marcus Hale will send the shift handover report round today, no rush.</v>

00:07:58.449 --> 00:07:59.649
<v Marcus Hale>Yep.</v>

00:08:00.579 --> 00:08:08.980
<v Sarah Okafor>And the risk assessment for work on the line 2 interlock on the 3rd is top priority please, but currently unowned, so it's flagged.</v>

00:08:11.259 --> 00:08:12.459
<v Fiona Doyle>Marked red.</v>

00:08:13.720 --> 00:08:14.920
<v Callum Reid>Sounds right.</v>

00:08:16.910 --> 00:08:19.009
<v Sarah Okafor>Nice one. Thanks everyone, crack on.</v>
